&lt;h2>Overview&lt;span class="hx-absolute -hx-mt-20" id="overview">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#overview" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h2>&lt;p>Clone of the ALSA RAVENNA/AES67 driver originally provided by &lt;strong>Merging Technologies&lt;/strong>. This Linux kernel module (LKM) enables the &lt;strong>RAVENNA&lt;/strong> network audio transport protocol (compatible with &lt;strong>AES67&lt;/strong>) within the ALSA subsystem on Linux.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>RAVENNA/AES67 is a professional audio-over-IP transport standard used in studios, concert halls and broadcast installations.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2>Features&lt;span class="hx-absolute -hx-mt-20" id="features">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#features" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h2>&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Linux kernel module (Loadable Kernel Module)&lt;/li>
&lt;li>RAVENNA/AES67 audio transport over IP&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Native ALSA integration&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Compatible with Merging Technologies equipment and other AES67 devices&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h2>Status&lt;span class="hx-absolute -hx-mt-20" id="status">&lt;/span>
&lt;a href="#status" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section">&lt;/a>&lt;/h2>&lt;p>⭐ &lt;strong>53 stars&lt;/strong> · 10 forks&lt;/p>
